From baf4e4d174c13730686d8fb00bc9fb2273b446ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 15:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix credit-assignment bug and resize PPO hyperparameters

The critic never saw a blocked (-1 reward) transition: env/environment.py
returned early on an infeasible mask before building state, and
training/simulator.py only buffered action-bearing steps, so blocking was
structurally invisible to the learner regardless of hyperparameters. Now
every arrival (blocked or not) gets a state + critic value, PPOAgent.update
runs GAE(lambda) with bootstrapping over the full trajectory, and the
policy loss/ratio stay restricted to action-bearing steps only.

Also: delete the epsilon-greedy branch from PPOAgent.select (it recorded
the target policy's log_prob for a uniform-behaviour action, corrupting
PPO's importance ratio), add running observation normalization, add the
previously-missing PPO fields (entropy_coef, gae_lambda, minibatch_size,
max_grad_norm, normalize_advantages, target_kl) with minibatched updates,
fix EpisodeMetrics' hardcoded gamma=0.99 to track the configured gamma,
and checkpoint on a rolling mean of BP instead of a single noisy episode.

Resize learning hyperparameters per docs/training_diagnosis.md section 5:
gamma 0.95->0.99, learning_rate 1e-5->3e-4, hidden_sizes (128,128)->
(256,256), buffer_size 64->2048, requests_per_episode 1500->3000, and
extend the evaluation arrival-rate sweep to 10-100.

Separately, core/topology.py's load_topology() ignored its path argument
and always returned a hardcoded 12-node graph, silently overriding
whatever topology_path a config specified (a working JSON-loading
implementation was sitting commented out below it). Restored it, since a
wrong topology makes every blocking measurement meaningless. Also fixed a
stale sseon_qkd_drl.* import in tests/test_state.py and a pyproject.toml
testpaths/package-discovery mismatch with the repo's actual flat layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
